title: Match-3 levels
intro: Points for every gem cleared, a move limit, and goals that win the level or lose it. No code.
project: Empty | Gem Quest

chapter: Score, moves and goals | The Match Board's Score and Goals
create: Match Board
set: MatchBoard.Seed = 152
explain: field:MatchBoard.Points | Points | Each gem cleared scores ten points, and more along a chain: gems in the second clear after a swap score double, the third triple.
set: MatchBoard.Moves = 3
explain: field:MatchBoard.Moves | Moves | Three swaps to play with.
set: MatchBoard.TargetScore = 150
explain: field:MatchBoard.TargetScore | Target Score | And a score of a hundred and fifty to reach.
explain: field:MatchBoard.Collect | Collect | Collect asks for gems of a kind to clear instead, or as well: twenty of one kind, fifteen of another.
explain: field:MatchBoard.WinMessage | Win Message | Meet the goals and the board sends Level Complete. Run out of moves first and it sends Out of Moves. Either way, no more swaps.
deselect
create: Text
rename: Score
add: ScreenAnchor
set: ScreenAnchor.Anchor = Top
set: ScreenAnchor.Offset = 0, -0.5
add: Counter
set: Counter.Track = *
set: Counter.Output = Score
set: Counter.Format = Score: {0} / {2}
explain: field:Counter.Output | Score | A counter counting the output Score shows the board's score, and brace two is the score to reach.
deselect
create: Text
rename: Moves
add: ScreenAnchor
set: ScreenAnchor.Anchor = Bottom
set: ScreenAnchor.Offset = 0, 0.5
add: Counter
set: Counter.Track = *
set: Counter.Output = Moves
set: Counter.Format = Moves left: {3}
explain: field:Counter.Output | Moves | The output Moves counts the board's swaps, and brace three is how many are left. Cleared, with a tile number after it, does the same for the gems of one kind cleared.
deselect
create: Panel
rename: Won
set: Panel.OpenMessage = Level Complete
create: Text
rename: Won Text
set: Text.Value = Level complete!
explain: entity:Won | A panel for the win | And a panel that opens on Level Complete.

chapter: Play the level | Three moves to score a hundred and fifty
play
wait: 0.5
expectvalue: Score.Text.Value = Score: 0 / 150
expectvalue: Moves.Text.Value = Moves left: 3
say: Click a gem, then the one beside it.
gameclick: -0.5, 2.5
wait: 0.3
gameclick: 0.5, 2.5
wait: 2
expectvalue: Board.MatchBoard.Score = 90
expectvalue: Score.Text.Value = Score: 90 / 150
expectvalue: Moves.Text.Value = Moves left: 2
explain: game | A chain scores more | Three gems cleared for thirty points, then three that landed in a line for sixty more, double along the chain. Two moves left.
say: One more swap, with the keys this time.
tap: Right
wait: 0.3
tap: Right
wait: 0.3
tap: Right
wait: 0.3
tap: Up
wait: 0.4
tap: Space
wait: 0.4
tap: Down
waitfor: Won Text | 6
expectvalue: Board.MatchBoard.Swaps = 2
explain: game | Level complete | Past a hundred and fifty with a move to spare: once the board comes to rest the level is won, and the panel opens.
stop
say: That's a match-3 level with no code. The score, swaps and gems cleared are saved with the scene, so rewinding takes them back.
